    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Traction is the transportation process involving the rolling of large boulders along the riverbed.",
        "Saltation involves small pebbles bouncing along the riverbed.",
        "Suspension carries light, fine particles directly suspended within the water flow.",
        "Solution transports dissolved materials and chemical load in the river water.",
        "Deposition takes place when the velocity of the river decreases, leading to the settling of sediments."
      ],
